  "CI 77499":                                  { role: "Non classifié", description: "Black Iron Oxide is thesuper common inorganic(as in no carbon atom in the molecule)pigmentthat controls the darkness of your foundation or gives the blackness to your mascara. Blended with red and black iron oxides, it is essential in all \"flesh-toned\" makeup products." },
  "CI 77510":                                  { role: "Non classifié", description: "An inorganic (as in no carbon in its molecule)pigmentthat has avery intense, dark blue color. It is not permitted in lip products in the US, and only the version Ferric Ammonium Ferrocyanide is permitted in the EU." },
